    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 1,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "There are many stories about Michael Sullivan. Some say he was a decent man. Some say there was no good in him at all. But I once spent six weeks on the road with him in the winter of 1931."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 1,
        "line": 566,
        "text": "But I lived a lifetime before that, in those six weeks on the road, in the winter of nineteen thirty-one. When people ask me if Michael Sullivan was a good man, or if there was just no good in him at all, I always give the same answer. I just tell them... he was my father."
      }
    },
